00:10:06.244 --> 00:10:10.002
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:13.566
After Sarah decides that the kids have had enough freaky videotape for one night

00:10:13.588 --> 00:10:16.626
and sends them to bed, the real Art proves that he's not limited to

00:10:16.648 --> 00:10:20.500
just the world of fiction by hiding in Tia's closet and freaking her out.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.660
-[Sarah] No, it's just make believe.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:26.446
-[Sarah] Demons, witches, monsters that doesn't exist.

00:10:26.558 --> 00:10:29.766
-[Tia] But he wasn't really a monster, if you think about it.

00:10:29.868 --> 00:10:32.418
-[Tia] Like a vampire or werewolf.

00:10:32.514 --> 00:10:34.450
-[Tia] He was just a man in a costume.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:38.994
-[Tia] Someone like that could really exist, right? Like a serial killer.

00:10:39.042 --> 00:10:40.834
This seems intentional.

00:10:40.882 --> 00:10:44.038
The suggestion that Art might be human actually makes him scarier in the

00:10:44.044 --> 00:10:44.630
real world.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.818
Sarah goes back downstairs to watch more of the videotape in what I assume is

00:10:47.824 --> 00:10:50.998
the one house in America that still had a VCR hooked up in 2013.

00:10:51.094 --> 00:10:54.634
I guess finding a DVD or Blu-Ray in your Halloween candy isn't nearly as creepy.

00:10:54.672 --> 00:10:57.486
Maybe Art would have reached more people with a Blu-Ray that just

00:10:57.508 --> 00:11:00.618
comes in a VHS box, like these Stranger Things physical releases.

00:11:00.714 --> 00:11:03.774
At least that would explain why we have a VHS tape displaying video in widescreen.

00:11:03.812 --> 00:11:07.326
Anyways, the second short on the tape barely features

00:11:07.348 --> 00:11:07.854
Art the Clown at all.

00:11:07.892 --> 00:11:09.726
He's very much shoehorned into this story.

00:11:09.828 --> 00:11:12.686
Basically, at the beginning, a woman mentions her Artist's husband,

00:11:12.708 --> 00:11:15.334
Who painted a terrible face that earned him some attention in the Art world.

00:11:15.372 --> 00:11:17.638
The husband claims that he must have been in some kind of trance when he

00:11:17.644 --> 00:11:19.622
painted the face because he doesn't remember doing it.

00:11:19.676 --> 00:11:22.514
Long story short, a rather short film, even shorter.

00:11:22.562 --> 00:11:25.126
When the painting of the terrible face is revealed at the end,

00:11:25.148 --> 00:11:27.158
it's Art the Clown doing his signature smiling face.

00:11:27.244 --> 00:11:30.054
The whole painting feels a little bit forced, but it's worth talking about

00:11:30.092 --> 00:11:32.898
because it introduces a different kind of supernatural element to Art's character. 

00:11:32.914 --> 00:11:36.466
Can Art the Clown possess people like a demon?

00:11:36.498 --> 00:11:40.030
Does he possess the minds of Artists exclusively? Could this be why he's named Art in the first place? 

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:42.938
This might seem like a little bit of a stretch, but this isn't

00:11:42.954 --> 00:11:45.386
the last time that Art will torture the mind of an artist.

00:11:45.498 --> 00:11:48.906
Back in the real world, Sarah is disturbed by Art's smiling face and turns

00:11:48.938 --> 00:11:49.534
the movie off.

00:11:49.572 --> 00:11:52.286
She hears something upstairs and assumes it's the kids, but when she goes to

00:11:52.308 --> 00:11:54.578
check on them, Timmy claims that they've been in bed the whole time and

00:11:54.584 --> 00:11:57.042
tells Sarah to stop checking on them every five minutes.

00:11:57.176 --> 00:12:01.810
I heard you creeping around outside the door and turning the handle.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.754
Again, we don't actually see Art in the house, but it's obvious that he's probably

00:12:04.792 --> 00:12:07.278
lingering around, and Sarah starts to get freaked out herself.

00:12:07.374 --> 00:12:10.962
If this terrified babysitter business seems familiar, it may be because Laurie Strode

00:12:11.026 --> 00:12:13.894
Was babysitting Tommy Doyle and Lindsay Wallace when she first

00:12:13.932 --> 00:12:15.826
encountered Michael Myers in Halloween.

00:12:15.938 --> 00:12:19.014
Sarah's curiosity outweighs her fright, however, because she goes back

00:12:19.052 --> 00:12:20.642
downstairs to watch more of the tape.

00:12:20.706 --> 00:12:24.082
The third and final short film is the Terrifier short film from 2011.

00:12:24.146 --> 00:12:26.562
It's finally Art the Clown's time to take center stage.

00:12:26.626 --> 00:12:29.138
The first time we see Art in the short, he's getting kicked out of a gas

00:12:29.154 --> 00:12:31.962
station for supposed smearing piss and s**t all over the walls.

00:12:32.026 --> 00:12:34.826
Not the last time he would destroy a public restroom, and he notices a woman

00:12:34.858 --> 00:12:36.350
filling up gas as he walks away.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.002
Art looks slightly different here than he did in the 9th circle.

00:12:39.066 --> 00:12:42.238
His neck is no longer visible, his mask is longer and tied down with a

00:12:42.244 --> 00:12:44.922
collar of sorts, and he's got a more pronounced bump on his nose.

00:12:44.986 --> 00:12:48.034
Leone said that Art's new look in Terrifier was intended to make him look

00:12:48.072 --> 00:12:49.742
more zombie like and a little scarier.

00:12:49.806 --> 00:12:51.982
He also carries a much larger garbage bag.

00:12:52.046 --> 00:12:55.166
A little later, Art interrupts an interaction between the gas station

00:12:55.198 --> 00:12:57.902
attendant and the woman, who we learn is a costume designer.

00:12:57.966 --> 00:13:01.254
Art lures the attendant back inside the gas station to dismember and kill him.

00:13:01.292 --> 00:13:03.906
He's about halfway through beheading the guy when the costume designer

00:13:03.938 --> 00:13:05.718
stumbles into the scene and freaks out.

00:13:05.804 --> 00:13:06.662
And here it is.

00:13:06.716 --> 00:13:10.310
Art the Clown's very first documented act of horrific violence.

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:14.634
Keeping up with our Michael Myers comparison, let's look back at his first

00:13:14.672 --> 00:13:15.546
murder as well.

00:13:15.648 --> 00:13:19.254
It also took place on Halloween, and Michael was wearing a clown costume.

00:13:19.302 --> 00:13:21.718
Perhaps the most direct link between the two characters.

00:13:21.814 --> 00:13:25.178
The woman speeds away in her car and makes a frantic 911 call when she sees

00:13:25.194 --> 00:13:27.950
Art on the side of the road with a sign that says Circus.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:32.398
-[Costume Designer] That’s impossible. That’s f*cking impossible!

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:33.342
She's right.

00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:34.362
That would be impossible.

00:13:34.426 --> 00:13:37.326
And this is her first piece of evidence that Art possesses supernatural abilities,

00:13:37.358 --> 00:13:39.358
in this case, teleportation.

00:13:39.454 --> 00:13:42.242
After nearly crashing her car in panic, Art appears again.

00:13:42.296 --> 00:13:45.814
But apparently his supernatural abilities don't include opening

00:13:45.852 --> 00:13:46.470
locked car doors.

00:13:47.012 --> 00:13:55.341
(Art tries to open the locked door)

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.626
Art must have taken another victim earlier that night, because the costume

00:13:58.658 --> 00:14:02.002
girl comes across another motorist who is dismembered and defaced, literally.

00:14:02.066 --> 00:14:05.266
The faceless driver looks very similar to some of the witches

00:14:05.298 --> 00:14:08.418
featured in the 9th Circle, though I don't necessarily think the filmmakers

00:14:08.434 --> 00:14:11.278
are trying to say that Art's victims are banished to the hell depicted in

00:14:11.284 --> 00:14:11.962
the 9th Circle.

00:14:12.026 --> 00:14:15.198
The costume designer drives away yet again, but little does she know

00:14:15.204 --> 00:14:17.310
Art the Clown has stowed away in the backseat of her car.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.886
You can see she just leaves the door open when she goes to check on the

00:14:19.908 --> 00:14:20.542
other car.

00:14:20.676 --> 00:14:24.318
Not the smartest, but one thing is for sure Art's attempt to suffocate the

00:14:24.324 --> 00:14:27.214
costume designer by pulling saran wrap around her face is a dumb one.

00:14:27.252 --> 00:14:29.954
She punctures a hole in the saran wrap and slams on the brakes,

00:14:29.992 --> 00:14:31.534
sending Art flying headfirst into the dashboard.

00:14:31.582 --> 00:14:34.606
Art is stunned, giving her time to find a brief refuge in the woods,

00:14:34.638 --> 00:14:35.822
locking herself in an old barn.

00:14:35.886 --> 00:14:38.866
We know Art is no match for a locked door, but that doesn't mean he can't

00:14:38.898 --> 00:14:40.790
find other means of entry.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:45.846
Art emerges from the ground and attacks the costume designer with what would

00:14:45.868 --> 00:14:49.158
become one of his favorite weapons a bunch of sharp objects attached to a chain.

00:14:49.164 --> 00:14:52.306
However, the chain breaks faster than a breath of the wild weapon,

00:14:52.338 --> 00:14:55.306
and as Art struggles with it, the costume designer grabs a small blade and

00:14:55.328 --> 00:14:57.738
sticks it in his eye before jamming a knife in his back.

00:14:57.824 --> 00:15:01.146
She escapes and manages to flag down a vehicle driven by a young man with a face.

00:15:01.168 --> 00:15:04.822
Art rises from the ground and, with a knife still in his back,

00:15:04.886 --> 00:15:06.142
Chases after her in a car of his own.

00:15:06.196 --> 00:15:07.754
He's a surprisingly skilled driver.

00:15:07.802 --> 00:15:10.414
He pulls up next to them and shoots the driver in the head, all while

00:15:10.452 --> 00:15:11.982
silently laughing at what he's done.

00:15:12.036 --> 00:15:15.038
Art's use of a firearm is a departure from what you'd normally expect from a slasher.

00:15:15.044 --> 00:15:18.430
Michael Myers used a variety of weapons, but never a gun.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:21.746
Leone has stated in interviews that his choice to allow Art the Clown to use

00:15:21.768 --> 00:15:22.914
guns is a deliberate one.

00:15:22.952 --> 00:15:25.554
It's part of his larger mission to continually break the rules and

00:15:25.592 --> 00:15:27.982
expectations with Art in order to keep him unpredictable.

00:15:28.046 --> 00:15:30.558
And it certainly seems to have caught his victim by surprise.

00:15:30.654 --> 00:15:33.954
She careens off the road into a tree, and Art takes her back to his lair,

00:15:34.002 --> 00:15:36.742
where she wakes up on a surgical table to find that he's been hard at work

00:15:36.796 --> 00:15:37.846
mutilating her body.

00:15:37.948 --> 00:15:41.286
He points and laughs at her as she discovers that her limbs and breasts have

00:15:41.308 --> 00:15:44.774
been removed and several words have been carved into her like pig and many

00:15:44.812 --> 00:15:47.682
others that may rhyme with punt, mitch, and glut.

00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:50.170
And this is where the Terrifier short ends.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.226
So what do we learn about Art here? We know he has some supernatural abilities

00:15:53.258 --> 00:15:55.614
and that locked doors are a weakness for him.

00:15:55.652 --> 00:15:58.654
He killed two men and a faceless third person whose gender we can't say for sure.

00:15:58.692 --> 00:16:01.386
The thing that I notice is how he really locked in on the costume

00:16:01.418 --> 00:16:02.734
designer the moment he saw her.

00:16:02.772 --> 00:16:06.106
He hunted her down, tortured her, and carved some very female targeted

00:16:06.138 --> 00:16:07.370
insults into her flesh.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:10.754
So does this mean that Art has a problem with women in particular?

00:16:10.792 --> 00:16:14.398
Is he less the Michael Myers of his generation and more the Elliot Roger?

00:16:14.414 --> 00:16:17.266
I don't know if there's enough evidence to say for sure, but it sure seems like it,

00:16:17.288 --> 00:16:20.402
Based on these first couple of appearances.

00:16:20.466 --> 00:16:22.422
He has a tendency to target women and just kill the men that get in the way.

00:16:22.476 --> 00:16:25.906
Michael Myers is very much the same way, going after Laurie Strode,

00:16:25.938 --> 00:16:29.638
Jamie Lloyd, Kara Strode, and Alison Nelson as his main targets throughout the years,

00:16:29.638 --> 00:16:32.630
but also stabbing anyone else who gets in his way, male or female.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:36.122
Art would continue to primarily target female victims going forward,

00:16:36.176 --> 00:16:37.734
But that's also most horror movies.

00:16:37.782 --> 00:16:40.534
So this text carved into the costume designer is probably the strongest

00:16:40.582 --> 00:16:41.498
evidence we have.

00:16:41.584 --> 00:16:44.766
What is clear is that with Art the Clown, your best bet is to expect the unexpected.

00:16:44.788 --> 00:16:48.042
This is especially true when he makes his first appearance

00:16:48.106 --> 00:16:51.200
outside the VHS tape and in the real world.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:54.201
(Impact)

00:16:56.201 --> 00:17:00.230
♪ Creepy Music ♪

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:03.566
Sarah, the babysitter, scrambles to turn off the TV, but the remote won't work.

00:17:03.598 --> 00:17:07.326
Art saws a body and stares directly through the television at Sarah.

00:17:07.358 --> 00:17:10.034
He's blurring the lines that separate the real world from the world within

00:17:10.072 --> 00:17:10.766
the videotape.

00:17:10.798 --> 00:17:12.242
And this is just the beginning.

00:17:12.306 --> 00:17:14.102
She turns off the TV and answers the phone.

00:17:14.156 --> 00:17:16.918
The woman on the other end screams for help and yells about a murder at a

00:17:16.924 --> 00:17:17.474
gas station.

00:17:17.522 --> 00:17:20.502
It's the costume designer making the exact same 911 call that she made in

00:17:20.502 --> 00:17:21.362
the movie.

00:17:21.362 --> 00:17:24.754
The TV suddenly turns back on, and Art the Clown now appears to be literally

00:17:24.802 --> 00:17:25.942
trapped inside of it.

00:17:25.996 --> 00:17:29.078
After seemingly trying to break out of the TV screen, she sees the image of

00:17:29.084 --> 00:17:32.506
the living room that she stand again with Art sitting behind her,

00:17:32.538 --> 00:17:33.134
seemingly to reflect this.

00:17:33.172 --> 00:17:36.718
He materializes in the real world, but Sarah smashes the tape before he can

00:17:36.724 --> 00:17:38.506
make contact with her, and he disappears.

00:17:38.618 --> 00:17:42.154
Tia screams upstairs, and Sarah goes to check on her, but what she finds

00:17:42.202 --> 00:17:44.318
turns her entire world inside out.

00:17:44.404 --> 00:17:48.178
Art stands at the top of the stairs, laughing and covered in splats of red.

00:17:48.264 --> 00:17:51.378
In this instance, the real world takes on the same grainy look as the

00:17:51.384 --> 00:17:54.942
Terrifier short film, indicating that Sarah is now in the horror movie.

00:17:55.006 --> 00:17:57.922
And as she saw in the VHS tape, anything goes.

00:17:58.056 --> 00:18:01.062
Art points to the children's bedroom, where Sarah discovers the kids

00:18:01.116 --> 00:18:02.802
beheaded and chopped to pieces.

00:18:02.866 --> 00:18:06.146
Art signs his name and blood on the bedroom wall, effectively introducing

00:18:06.178 --> 00:18:08.610
himself and perhaps signing his latest masterpiece.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.306
Maybe this is why he's called Art, because he makes spectacles of his kills

00:18:12.338 --> 00:18:13.978
and signs them like works of Art.

00:18:14.064 --> 00:18:16.954
I certainly think it's a work of Art, but then again, have you seen my apartment.

00:18:16.992 --> 00:18:19.926
But interestingly, this is another thing that Art

00:18:19.958 --> 00:18:20.858
and Michael Myers have in common.

00:18:20.944 --> 00:18:24.054
Michael also likes to make Artwork out of his victims with extravagant

00:18:24.102 --> 00:18:25.514
displays and elaborate settings.

00:18:25.562 --> 00:18:28.026
Think about the scene from the first Halloween of one of his victims,

00:18:28.058 --> 00:18:29.834
arranged under the Judith Myers tombstone.

00:18:29.882 --> 00:18:33.114
The carousel display he set up in Halloween kills, or even his signature

00:18:33.162 --> 00:18:36.350
head tilt, almost as if he's admiring his kills in an Art gallery.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.954
Michael Myers doesn't sign his work.

00:18:37.992 --> 00:18:41.220
But then again, Haddonfield is a small town and people know his name.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.753
(Numerous people saying MICHAEL)

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:48.274
This final sequence demonstrates that Art the Clown exists not just within

00:18:48.312 --> 00:18:51.318
the short films on the videotape, but also in the real world within the moviee.

00:18:51.324 --> 00:18:54.162
And to put another hat on this hat on a hat.

00:18:54.226 --> 00:18:57.446
As this story comes to an end, Art invades the screen of the viewer the same

00:18:57.468 --> 00:18:59.698
way he invaded Sarah's screen just moments earlier.

00:18:59.794 --> 00:19:03.286
This, The Ring-esque move suggests that Art may exist in our real world as well.

00:19:03.308 --> 00:19:06.138
It's a final touch that adds a little bit more mystique to Art the Clown.

00:19:06.144 --> 00:19:10.358
Six years pass before Art makes his presence known again in 2019.

00:19:10.454 --> 00:19:14.026
You're probably asking yourself, if Terrifier came out in 2016,

00:19:14.048 --> 00:19:16.430
why does the movie take place in 2019? Let's break it down.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.674
Art always attacks on Halloween night, which of course bleeds into November 1st.

00:19:19.722 --> 00:19:23.518
In Terrifier, we see a cell phone that says it's Friday, November 1st.

00:19:23.604 --> 00:19:26.970
November 1st only falls on a Friday in 2013 or in 2019.

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:29.970
The next chapter of Art's story takes place exactly one year later.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.394
And in that story, in a child's bedroom, we see a poster for an album by

00:19:33.432 --> 00:19:34.894
Aenimus called A Dreamcatcher.

00:19:34.942 --> 00:19:38.466
This album came out in February of 2019, so it could be on a kid's wall in 2020.

00:19:38.488 --> 00:19:42.018
That being said, there's also this newspaper clipping which claims

00:19:42.034 --> 00:19:44.678
that it was published on Saturday, November 1st, which is obviously contradictory.

00:19:44.764 --> 00:19:47.446
So it's pretty likely that the filmmakers don't have a

00:19:47.468 --> 00:19:48.358
timeline in mind.

00:19:48.444 --> 00:19:51.638
But for our Horror History purposes, it's more likely that there could be a

00:19:51.644 --> 00:19:54.422
misprint on this newspaper rather than an error by the cell phone.

00:19:54.476 --> 00:19:55.906
So we're going to go with 2019.

00:19:56.018 --> 00:19:59.286
So with all of that being said, we still don't know exactly what Art was up

00:19:59.308 --> 00:20:00.894
to in the years since we last saw him.

00:20:00.932 --> 00:20:03.358
But it's safe to assume that he was out there butchering people on the

00:20:03.364 --> 00:20:06.142
Halloween nights between 2014 and 2019 as well.

00:20:06.196 --> 00:20:08.942
We know Art murdered a little girl at a carnival at some point before

00:20:08.996 --> 00:20:10.250
Halloween in 2019.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:12.894
After this happened, the carnival was just abandoned there, and it seems

00:20:12.932 --> 00:20:14.318
that Art is living out of it.

00:20:14.404 --> 00:20:17.758
We eventually see a bloody bathroom there in 2020, which basically serves as

00:20:17.764 --> 00:20:18.362
his lair.

00:20:18.426 --> 00:20:21.582
Based on the size of the mess, I'd say he took other victims here as well.

00:20:21.636 --> 00:20:23.870
It's too much carnage to have just been from one child.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:24.886
I would know.

00:20:25.028 --> 00:20:26.742
I mean, I mean, I wouldn't know.

00:20:26.796 --> 00:20:29.366
It's safe to assume that it happened on Halloween like the rest of his murders.

00:20:29.388 --> 00:20:32.518
As for the little girl, don't worry, we'll meet her soon.

00:20:32.604 --> 00:20:35.862
And while this probably isn't an intentional parallel or anything,

00:20:35.916 --> 00:20:39.366
Art living out of an abandoned carnival for the other 364 days a year leading up

00:20:39.388 --> 00:20:42.614
to Halloween feels a lot like Michael Myers hiding out in the sewers during

00:20:42.652 --> 00:20:43.618
Halloween Ends.

00:20:43.714 --> 00:20:46.758
Anyway, whatever he was doing in the meantime, by the time we see Art in 2019,

00:20:46.764 --> 00:20:48.438
he looks a little different.

00:20:48.524 --> 00:20:50.650
So let's pause for real world context.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:53.726
Mike Giannelli portrayed Art the Clown up to this point, and the thing about

00:20:53.748 --> 00:20:55.434
Giannelli is he's not an actor.

00:20:55.482 --> 00:20:58.074
He essentially got the part because he was a friend of the director Damian Leone,

00:20:58.122 --> 00:21:00.090
and more importantly, a good sport.

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:03.498
Leone said that when he cast the 9th Circle, his first priority was finding

00:21:03.514 --> 00:21:06.110
someone who would be comfortable sitting in makeup for 3 hours a day.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:09.858
Giannelli had helped Leone with his makeup test before, so he got the job.

00:21:09.944 --> 00:21:12.974
He wasn't an actor before portraying Art the Clown, and he hasn't acted since.

00:21:13.022 --> 00:21:16.126
For the first feature length, Terrifier, Leone put out a casting call,

00:21:16.158 --> 00:21:18.222
and that's how he met David Howard Thornton.

00:21:18.286 --> 00:21:21.298
Leone said that the difference between the two actors is that Mike Giannelli

00:21:21.314 --> 00:21:24.722
was a guy dressed as a clown, but David Howard Thornton actually is a clown.

00:21:24.786 --> 00:21:28.006
Leone describes Thornton as a real life Roger Rabbit with comedy and

00:21:28.028 --> 00:21:29.878
clowning chops and a lankier body.

00:21:29.964 --> 00:21:32.082
Okay, back to Halloween night in 2019.

00:21:32.146 --> 00:21:34.682
Art prepares for Halloween the same way that most of us do.

00:21:34.736 --> 00:21:35.942
By getting into costume.

00:21:36.006 --> 00:21:39.114
He puts on his gloves and face paint, and we actually get a distorted view

00:21:39.152 --> 00:21:40.250
of his unpainted face.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:43.562
This getting ready montage is probably the most compelling evidence that Art

00:21:43.616 --> 00:21:46.366
is actually supposed to be somewhat human, but there is still an

00:21:46.388 --> 00:21:47.390
air of mystery around him.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:50.734
A demon probably wouldn't have to take the time to get into costume, 

00:21:50.772 --> 00:21:53.450
but no normal human would ever have teeth quite like Art's.

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:56.730
Whatever the case, Art prepares a few choice weapons and heads out the door.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.438
Later that night, he's out in the streets, where he follows a pair of drunk girls,

00:21:59.454 --> 00:22:02.546
Dawn and Tara, into a pizza place where they attempt to sober up

00:22:02.568 --> 00:22:03.410
before driving home.

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:06.898
Art vies for Tara's attention and takes a selfie with Dawn before heading to

00:22:06.904 --> 00:22:08.946
the bathroom to make another horrific mess.

00:22:09.048 --> 00:22:12.006
I guess the events of the Terrifier short film really do come from

00:22:12.028 --> 00:22:12.690
a place of truth.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:16.854
This time, he even signs his name with the resources he has available.

00:22:16.972 --> 00:22:20.406
I guess a true artist can make something beautiful with whatever tools

00:22:20.428 --> 00:22:21.430
He or she has on hand.

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.946
And I'm not just saying that because I've used the same camera for every

00:22:23.968 --> 00:22:25.146
episode of Horror History.

00:22:25.248 --> 00:22:28.474
Art slashes the tires on the girl's car and heads back to the pizza place,

00:22:28.512 --> 00:22:31.386
where he beheads the restaurant owner and kills the pizza cook, whose last

00:22:31.408 --> 00:22:34.426
act on earth, aside from getting stabbed in the face a thousand times, 

00:22:34.448 --> 00:22:35.917
Was cleaning up Art's excrement.

00:22:35.917 --> 00:22:37.758
Dude didn't exactly go out on top.

00:22:37.844 --> 00:22:40.782
While waiting for a ride, Tara heads inside of a creepy apartment building

00:22:40.836 --> 00:22:43.370
to use the bathroom, leaving Dawn to wait in the car alone.

00:22:43.450 --> 00:22:46.151
A breaking news alert mentions the murders in the pizza restaurant, and the

00:22:46.151 --> 00:22:48.273
details are especially troubling. 

00:22:48.273 --> 00:22:54.542
-[Reporter] Police are on the lookout for a tall thin man wearing a 
black and white clown costume and carrying a large garbage bag. 

00:22:54.606 --> 00:22:58.118
But before Dawn can properly process this, Art pops in next door in the

00:22:58.124 --> 00:22:59.106
passenger seats.

00:22:59.218 --> 00:22:59.862
-[Dawn] Oh, my God.

00:22:59.916 --> 00:23:02.390
-[Dawn] You're never gonna believe what I just heard on the radio.

00:23:05.267 --> 00:23:05.927
(Screams)

00:23:06.010 --> 00:23:09.826
As much as I'd like to ream yet another character for leaving the car door unlocked,

00:23:09.858 --> 00:23:12.358
if I had a friend that was just running in somewhere to use the

00:23:12.364 --> 00:23:14.470
bathroom real quick, I probably wouldn't lock it either.

00:23:14.540 --> 00:23:17.878
He would keep her alive for now, but move her to an unused room inside the

00:23:17.884 --> 00:23:20.654
apartment complex, where she's stripped and hung upside down for the time being.

00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:23.742
Then, near the entrance, he finds Tara on her way out.

00:23:23.796 --> 00:23:26.394
Or rather, Tara finds him completely frozen.

00:23:26.442 --> 00:23:30.334
I think this is the most tense scene of Art's 2019 rampage, and like many

00:23:30.372 --> 00:23:33.306
aspects of his character, he does it by reversing expectations.

00:23:33.418 --> 00:23:36.346
While other villains might go for a scare with fast movement and loud noises,

00:23:36.378 --> 00:23:39.150
it is the lack of movement here that is unsettling.

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:42.222
That's why I brought up the importance of casting David Howard Thornton.

00:23:42.286 --> 00:23:45.470
His clown and mime skills translate really well to suspense and horror.

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:48.354
After breaking the standstill, he chases her into some kind of indoor car lot.

00:23:48.392 --> 00:23:51.734
But Art, like Michael Myers, doesn't really run, relying on being

00:23:51.772 --> 00:23:53.798
methodical and persistent rather than quick.

00:23:53.884 --> 00:23:57.014
It's part of the psychology of what makes him creepy, which I'll expand on

00:23:57.052 --> 00:23:57.750
in a little bit.

00:23:57.820 --> 00:24:01.126
He eventually tracks Tara down and slices her ankles, but she manages to

00:24:01.148 --> 00:24:03.876
stab him in the side and escape, just before he can gouge her eyes out.

00:24:04.028 --> 00:24:05.583
Art searches for her yet again.

00:24:05.884 --> 00:24:08.706
One interesting thing about Art's stalking is that he seems to be following

00:24:08.738 --> 00:24:09.238
her scent.

00:24:09.266 --> 00:24:12.174
That's just a minor specific, but it's one of the many traits that make him

00:24:12.212 --> 00:24:13.438
a little bit more than human.

00:24:13.524 --> 00:24:16.202
When he eventually catches up to Tara, he injects her with a sedative

00:24:16.266 --> 00:24:18.371
before she can get the attention of the exterminator, who had let her into

00:24:18.371 --> 00:24:19.060
the building.

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:22.494
Art takes Tara to another area, where he ties her up and toys with her,

00:24:22.532 --> 00:24:24.878
feigning several attacks with an axe, then a saw.

00:24:24.964 --> 00:24:26.762
He seems to really get off on her fear.

00:24:26.826 --> 00:24:30.306
Eventually, he backs off, and just for a second, it seems that Art may be

00:24:30.328 --> 00:24:32.574
showing Tara a little bit of uncharacteristic mercy.

00:24:32.622 --> 00:24:34.274
But of course, that's not the case.

00:24:34.392 --> 00:24:37.926
She would soon find that she is his literal captive audience and that the

00:24:37.948 --> 00:24:40.390
show was only just beginning.

00:24:40.390 --> 00:24:41.843
(Impact)

00:24:45.911 --> 00:24:49.142
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:50.742
Art walks across the room where,

00:24:50.796 --> 00:24:54.534
Ever the showman, he tears down a sheet to reveal Dawn hanging upside

00:24:54.582 --> 00:24:55.910
down with her legs apart.

00:24:55.990 --> 00:24:58.954
She is gagged and topless with her hands tied behind her back.

00:24:59.072 --> 00:25:02.870
Starting between her legs, he saws her in half, hot dog style.

00:25:02.950 --> 00:25:06.206
This is arguably one of the most brutal scenes of all time.

00:25:06.308 --> 00:25:09.114
As he saws, he continually checks in on Tara, laughing, all the while.

00:25:09.162 --> 00:25:11.182
Art is putting on a show.

00:25:11.236 --> 00:25:14.046
And the fact that he forces Tara to watch gives us a clue as to his motivation.

00:25:14.068 --> 00:25:17.426
Clearly, he set up this entire scenario so that he would have an audience.

00:25:17.448 --> 00:25:21.646
Maybe this is why he first appeared on that mysterious VHS tape

00:25:21.678 --> 00:25:22.542
six years prior.

00:25:22.606 --> 00:25:25.330
He wants people to watch him do the terrible things he does.

00:25:25.400 --> 00:25:27.122
He's a clown and a mime, after all.

00:25:27.176 --> 00:25:29.570
Clowns and mimes need audiences to perform in front of.

00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:32.758
Even the way the sheet is set up before revealing Dawn almost looks like a

00:25:32.764 --> 00:25:33.442
stage curtain.

00:25:33.506 --> 00:25:36.774
By making his kills more gruesome and hard for others to watch, 

00:25:36.812 --> 00:25:38.242
Art maybe gets more out of it for himself.

00:25:38.386 --> 00:25:40.962
Of course, with showmanship also comes drama.

00:25:41.026 --> 00:25:44.434
Tara manages to wiggle free and stab Art, and though he makes no audible scream,

00:25:44.482 --> 00:25:46.630
the pain is written all over his face.

00:25:46.700 --> 00:25:50.409
He bounces back quickly and follows her into a garage, where she beats him with a 2x4.

00:25:50.409 --> 00:25:53.152
Art is on the ropes, but just as it appears that he may actually be defeated,

00:25:53.152 --> 00:25:55.937
with one more blow to the head, he pulls out a gun and shoots her in the leg,

00:25:56.228 --> 00:25:59.102
in the side, and finally in the face.

00:25:59.236 --> 00:26:02.394
It's a cheap way out of the situation, but it does sort of follow Art's rule

00:26:02.442 --> 00:26:03.690
of doing the unexpected.

00:26:03.770 --> 00:26:06.798
He discovers Dawn's phone while reloading his gun in the other room, and he

00:26:06.804 --> 00:26:10.146
sees a text from Victoria, Tara's sister, who the two had called to pick them up.

00:26:10.168 --> 00:26:13.426
He may be mute, but apparently he understands English and how to use a smartphone,

00:26:13.448 --> 00:26:15.778
Instructing her to come around to the back.

00:26:15.864 --> 00:26:19.558
When he returns to Tara, who is somehow still alive despite being shot in the face,

00:26:19.564 --> 00:26:23.142
He finishes the job, but then notices someone is watching him.

00:26:23.196 --> 00:26:26.386
It's a strange, delusional woman who lives in the building and carries

00:26:26.418 --> 00:26:29.842
around a baby doll, taking care of it and acting as if it's a real baby.

00:26:29.906 --> 00:26:32.906
For some reason, she's listed in the credits as Cat Lady, even though she

00:26:32.928 --> 00:26:34.458
has a baby doll, not a cat.

00:26:34.544 --> 00:26:38.266
We do hear cat noises when Tara first runs into her, but that hardly seems

00:26:38.288 --> 00:26:41.146
like a justification for making that her whole entire thing.

00:26:41.248 --> 00:26:44.346
I do have a better theory about who she is, which I'll get to a little bit later.

00:26:44.368 --> 00:26:47.886
On the way to reach the so called Cat Lady, he crosses paths with the exterminator

00:26:47.908 --> 00:26:50.282
And smacks him unconscious with a hammer.

00:26:50.346 --> 00:26:53.438
Unlike the time Michael Myers killed a man in a jumpsuit and proceeded to

00:26:53.444 --> 00:26:56.446
steal that jumpsuit, Art lets the exterminator keep his clothing, but he

00:26:56.468 --> 00:26:58.706
would be due for an outfit change not long after.

00:26:58.808 --> 00:27:02.226
Instead of killing the baby doll lady, he steals her doll and treats it like

00:27:02.248 --> 00:27:03.022
a real baby.

00:27:03.086 --> 00:27:05.700
And when she discovers this, she pleads with him.

00:27:06.090 --> 00:27:14.711
-[Cat Lady] Is there kindness in you? Somewhere in your heart? Have you ever felt a mother's touch?

00:27:14.711 --> 00:27:18.454
She touches him tenderly on the face, and he leans into it

00:27:18.492 --> 00:27:20.150
and starts sucking his thumb.

00:27:22.010 --> 00:27:24.586
I don't know what the fuck that's all about, but I think it's safe to say

00:27:24.608 --> 00:27:26.730
that Art does indeed have issues with women.

00:27:26.800 --> 00:27:29.386
And while we probably won't ever get a backstory on how these issues came about,

00:27:29.408 --> 00:27:31.894
We can assume that they stem from some kind of trauma.

00:27:31.942 --> 00:27:34.938
Let's take his 1970s counterpart, Michael Myers, as an example.

00:27:35.024 --> 00:27:38.046
In a previous video, I discussed how Michael may have been traumatized by

00:27:38.068 --> 00:27:41.358
seeing his sister Judith perform s*xual acts when he was young, and this was

00:27:41.364 --> 00:27:44.446
the root of all of his issues and likely the motivation behind killing her

00:27:44.468 --> 00:27:46.058
in the opening of the original Halloween.

00:27:46.154 --> 00:27:49.758
It seems that whatever the cause, Art's issues around women go even crazier

00:27:49.854 --> 00:27:53.618
because he cuts off the baby lady's scalp and breast to turn himself into a

00:27:53.624 --> 00:27:57.026
maternal figure, which is how he greets Tara's sister, Victoria, when she comes

00:27:57.048 --> 00:27:58.222
into the building to search.

00:27:58.286 --> 00:28:01.526
Art does a Bugs Bunny pretty lady routine before attempting to break into

00:28:01.548 --> 00:28:03.442
the locked closet where Victoria's hiding.

00:28:03.506 --> 00:28:06.534
Once again, he struggles with the locked door before going outside to

00:28:06.572 --> 00:28:09.282
decapitate the exterminator's co-worker who had come for backup.

00:28:09.346 --> 00:28:11.522
He pulls the guy's head off without much difficulty.

00:28:11.586 --> 00:28:13.994
Honestly, if Art hadn't gotten to him, the guy's head was probably coming

00:28:14.032 --> 00:28:15.626
off before long one way or another.

00:28:15.728 --> 00:28:18.474
Back in the warehouse, he sneaks up on Victoria and tries the old

00:28:18.512 --> 00:28:21.706
suffocation via saran wrap routine, just like in the Terrifier short.

00:28:21.808 --> 00:28:25.018
It takes a while, but like the woman in the short, Victoria realizes she can

00:28:25.024 --> 00:28:26.074
tear a hole in the plastic.

00:28:26.122 --> 00:28:30.126
And I love how dumbfounded Art looks that his plan failed so close, and she

00:28:30.148 --> 00:28:33.066
uses this moment of confusion to stab him in the foot with a giant nail

00:28:33.098 --> 00:28:33.918
that's lying around.

00:28:34.004 --> 00:28:37.170
The chase continues into seedier and seedier looking areas of the supposed

00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:38.110
apartment complex.

00:28:38.190 --> 00:28:41.634
Victoria eventually discovers Tara's body decorated with the circus sign

00:28:41.672 --> 00:28:44.926
from the short film, but Art finds her and whips her with his classic chain

00:28:44.958 --> 00:28:48.574
full of sharp objects, not realizing the exterminator, that is the original

00:28:48.622 --> 00:28:51.286
exterminator is sneaking up behind him to knock him out.

00:28:51.388 --> 00:28:54.406
After regaining consciousness, Art catches up with him and stomps his face

00:28:54.428 --> 00:28:55.682
in with his big clown shoes.

00:28:55.746 --> 00:28:59.666
Who's the exterminator now, Mike? The last person to go after is Victoria,

00:28:59.698 --> 00:29:02.822
but she stabs him in the eye and escapes into some kind of restricted area

00:29:02.876 --> 00:29:05.894
with big swinging doors, kind of like the barn doors from the short film.

00:29:05.942 --> 00:29:08.966
Art can't squeeze through, once again proving his inability to pick a lock

00:29:08.998 --> 00:29:11.014
to be his greatest and most exploited weakness.

00:29:11.062 --> 00:29:14.486
So he's left to improvise the last time we saw him burrow under the ground.

00:29:14.518 --> 00:29:17.226
But that was just the short film, so it's hard to say if that's realistic

00:29:17.258 --> 00:29:17.758
for him.

00:29:17.780 --> 00:29:19.562
This time, he opts for a simpler solution.

00:29:19.626 --> 00:29:22.442
He steals the exterminator's truck and drives it right through the door,

00:29:22.506 --> 00:29:24.090
knocking Victoria out cold.

00:29:24.170 --> 00:29:27.378
This is the second time he's driven a car, which begs the question,

00:29:27.384 --> 00:29:29.168
Who the hell gave this guy a license?

00:29:29.168 --> 00:29:31.864
Strangely enough, Michael Myers also knew how to drive.

00:29:31.864 --> 00:29:35.054
In the very first Halloween, he escapes from a mental institution and drives

00:29:35.102 --> 00:29:36.658
150 miles back home.

00:29:36.744 --> 00:29:38.930
There have been entire articles written about this.

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:41.506
When did Michael learn how to drive? When he spent his life at a mental institution.

00:29:41.538 --> 00:29:45.174
Between this and his ability to use a cell phone,

00:29:45.212 --> 00:29:46.070
Art seems more and more human.

00:29:46.140 --> 00:29:47.926
But that would all change before long.

00:29:48.028 --> 00:29:49.314
First, he goes cannibal.

00:29:49.362 --> 00:29:52.786
He climbs on top of the unconscious Victoria and licks the fresh strawberry

00:29:52.818 --> 00:29:54.006
syrup off of her face.

00:29:54.108 --> 00:29:57.446
He seems a little bit more invested than usual, taking the time to enjoy the taste,

00:29:57.468 --> 00:30:00.398
then fully chowing down on her face as the police arrive.

00:30:00.484 --> 00:30:03.278
He doesn't really react to the police until they're right on top of him with

00:30:03.284 --> 00:30:04.154
their guns drawn.

00:30:04.202 --> 00:30:06.990
And even then, he seems more annoyed than he is afraid of them.

00:30:07.060 --> 00:30:10.398
A locked cell probably qualifies as a locked door that Art won't be able to

00:30:10.404 --> 00:30:14.174
get out of, so he opts for the alternative, the last trick up his sleeve, or

00:30:14.212 --> 00:30:15.722
more accurately, up his sock.

00:30:15.786 --> 00:30:19.694
He takes out his pistol and shoots himself in the face and dies.

00:30:19.822 --> 00:30:22.126
Of course, that's not how it ends.

00:30:22.238 --> 00:30:25.806
For the entirety of his story in Terrifier, which is probably most people's

00:30:25.838 --> 00:30:28.606
first exposure to Art the Clown, there's nothing to suggest that he's

00:30:28.638 --> 00:30:31.650
anything more than a psychotic serial killer wearing a clown costume.

00:30:31.730 --> 00:30:35.154
He can get hurt, but he's resilient and he keeps coming after his victims.

00:30:35.202 --> 00:30:37.858
Michael Myers is handled the exact same way in Halloween.

00:30:37.954 --> 00:30:41.654
That is, until the end, when he takes a hail of bullets and somehow still

00:30:41.692 --> 00:30:43.498
disappears into the Haddonfield night.

00:30:43.584 --> 00:30:46.326
The final twist is that he's invincible, and this is one of the biggest

00:30:46.358 --> 00:30:48.122
characteristics that Art shares with him.

00:30:48.176 --> 00:30:51.306
So instead of jail, he's taken to the coroner's office alongside the

00:30:51.328 --> 00:30:52.922
exterminator whose head he stomped in.

00:30:52.976 --> 00:30:56.686
When Art's body bag is opened he's doing his signature smile, staring up at

00:30:56.708 --> 00:30:58.314
the coroner with his one remaining eye.

00:30:58.362 --> 00:31:01.546
The lights in the hospital flicker and electronics go haywire, indicating

00:31:01.578 --> 00:31:03.922
that there are indeed otherworldly powers at work here.

00:31:03.976 --> 00:31:06.260
Then he finishes the guy with this...

00:31:06.260 --> 00:31:11.281
(Art strangles the coroner)

00:31:11.590 --> 00:31:14.946
I somehow don't think it's a coincidence that Art sits up the exact same way

00:31:14.968 --> 00:31:17.572
Michael Myers does, after regenerating from a major injury.

00:31:17.572 --> 00:31:18.946
He would later slit the man's throat

00:31:18.946 --> 00:31:19.736
as well.

00:31:19.736 --> 00:31:22.514
When he checks out his injuries in the mirror, he kind of looks surprised

00:31:22.562 --> 00:31:26.722
and uses some of his brain juice to sign his name in the mirror.

00:31:26.786 --> 00:31:29.794
His reaction makes me think that this is the first time that he's respawned,

00:31:29.842 --> 00:31:31.462
and even he did not expect it.

00:31:31.516 --> 00:31:34.706
After smashing the guy's teeth out with a hammer, he pulls the coroner's eye

00:31:34.738 --> 00:31:37.926
straight out of its socket and places it into his own empty eye cavity to

00:31:37.948 --> 00:31:38.886
try it on for size.

00:31:38.988 --> 00:31:40.026
An eye for an eye.

00:31:40.098 --> 00:31:42.720
Or I guess more accurately, an eye for nothing.

00:31:42.720 --> 00:31:44.720
(Art turns and reveals his new eye)

00:31:45.090 --> 00:31:48.398
Victoria, by the way, does survive the incident and becomes something of a

00:31:48.404 --> 00:31:51.246
media sensation, partially due to the fact that she has no face.

00:31:51.348 --> 00:31:54.218
After an interview with a journalist known for her exploitative and

00:31:54.244 --> 00:31:57.422
sensational nature, she savagely attacks the journalist backstage.

00:31:57.486 --> 00:32:00.814
This shows that the evil force driving Art the Clown might be contagious,

00:32:00.862 --> 00:32:04.210
which sets the stage perfectly for Art's next chapter.

00:32:04.210 --> 00:32:05.211
(Impact)

00:32:08.948 --> 00:32:13.109
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:32:13.370 --> 00:32:16.726
After taking out the corner early in the morning on November 1st, 

00:32:16.748 --> 00:32:19.714
he scours his supplies and steals some fluoroantimonic acid, aka,

00:32:19.762 --> 00:32:21.958
The strongest, most corrosive acid in the world.

00:32:22.044 --> 00:32:24.666
It's better to have it and not need it than need it and not have it.

00:32:24.688 --> 00:32:26.586
You know? I'm sure he'll find a good use.

00:32:26.688 --> 00:32:29.814
Art evades the police again and heads to the laundromat, where he strips

00:32:29.862 --> 00:32:31.302
naked and washes his outfit.

00:32:31.366 --> 00:32:34.154
Because when you live in an abandoned carnival attraction, you gotta give up

00:32:34.192 --> 00:32:35.962
things like in-unit washer and dryer.

00:32:36.026 --> 00:32:39.102
The power in the laundromat goes off momentarily, and this is where Art

00:32:39.156 --> 00:32:40.158
meets a new friend.

00:32:40.244 --> 00:32:42.718
Her makeup, clothes and teeth look a lot like Art.

00:32:42.804 --> 00:32:45.214
In the credits, she's referred to as the Little Pale Girl.

00:32:45.252 --> 00:32:48.750
But based on this newspaper headline, her real name seems to be Emily Crane,

00:32:48.830 --> 00:32:52.098
the same little girl I mentioned before who Art kidnapped and murdered at

00:32:52.104 --> 00:32:54.206
the carnival sometime prior to 2019.

00:32:54.318 --> 00:32:57.158
Now, this might be a coincidence, but do you remember the Cat Lady with the baby doll from earlier?

00:32:57.164 --> 00:33:01.414
Well, guess what that baby doll's name was? 

00:33:01.452 --> 00:33:02.790
-[Cat Lady] This is my daughter, Emily.

00:33:03.450 --> 00:33:05.990
-[Cat Lady] Say hello to the pretty young lady.

00:33:07.050 --> 00:33:10.838
So if this isn't a coincidence, then the Cat Lady, who should be called the

00:33:10.844 --> 00:33:13.782
Baby Doll Lady is the mother of Emily Crane, aka.

00:33:13.846 --> 00:33:14.890
The Pale Little Girl.

00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:16.746
Art really did a number on that family.

00:33:16.848 --> 00:33:20.106
Either way, we know that the Pale Little Girl now mostly exists inside of Art's head,

00:33:20.128 --> 00:33:23.094
because when another man in the laundromat notices the bizarre scene,

00:33:23.142 --> 00:33:25.866
He sees only Art playing Patty cake by himself.

00:33:25.978 --> 00:33:28.894
The onlooker doesn't even get to tell anyone about this strange scene before

00:33:28.932 --> 00:33:31.162
Art puts a broom through his head and finishes his laundry.

00:33:31.226 --> 00:33:34.234
He does a remarkable job with his laundry, by the way, and then disappears

00:33:34.282 --> 00:33:35.166
for the next year.

00:33:35.268 --> 00:33:38.366
Over the course of that year, the legend of Art the Clown grew bigger than

00:33:38.388 --> 00:33:39.006
ever before.

00:33:39.108 --> 00:33:42.586
The events of 2019 are known as the Miles County Massacre, and the internet

00:33:42.618 --> 00:33:45.378
is a buzz with speculation about Art and what he's all about.

00:33:45.394 --> 00:33:48.086
There are even photos and sketches of him floating around online.

00:33:48.188 --> 00:33:51.046
We don't know exactly what Art himself was doing this time, but we do know

00:33:51.068 --> 00:33:53.926
that he's been plaguing the mind of at least one person, the father of the Shaw family,

00:33:53.948 --> 00:33:57.314
whose teenage daughter Sienna ended up being Art's main target the next Halloween.

00:33:57.362 --> 00:34:00.594
Sienna's dad had a brain tumor that kept it growing.

00:34:00.642 --> 00:34:04.166
It drove him to psychosis, and in his madness, he feverishly drew portraits

00:34:04.198 --> 00:34:07.274
of Art and his victims, then eventually went mad and killed himself by

00:34:07.312 --> 00:34:08.534
driving into a transformer.

00:34:08.582 --> 00:34:11.626
I would surmise that Art was the one who caused the brain tumor, or at least

00:34:11.648 --> 00:34:13.718
the dad's obsession with drawing him and his victim.

00:34:13.814 --> 00:34:17.098
Remember, in the second short film on the VHS tape, an Artist is possessed

00:34:17.114 --> 00:34:20.378
to draw a terrible face without having any recollection of it, and it turns

00:34:20.394 --> 00:34:21.614
out to be Art's face.

00:34:21.732 --> 00:34:25.534
Maybe Art has some ability to invade the dreams and imaginations of other artists.

00:34:25.572 --> 00:34:29.086
In fact, the night before Halloween, he seems to invade the dreams

00:34:29.118 --> 00:34:29.726
of Sienna.

00:34:29.758 --> 00:34:32.834
The dream takes place in a commercial set known as the clown cafe, where teenagers

00:34:32.872 --> 00:34:36.334
dressed like kids sing along to a very eerie song about the clown cafe

00:34:36.382 --> 00:34:38.862
which is actually just a food truck.

00:34:38.926 --> 00:34:42.566
Art rolls up on his tricycle and hands out treats, giving Sienna the gift of

00:34:42.588 --> 00:34:44.546
a human heart covered in worms and black blood.

00:34:44.578 --> 00:34:46.674
And this is where her dream becomes a nightmare.

00:34:46.722 --> 00:34:50.214
He pulls out a tommy gun and massacres the entire place, sets fire to everything,

00:34:50.252 --> 00:34:53.686
Then turns his flamethrower on Sienna, who shields herself with

00:34:53.708 --> 00:34:55.478
a sword once given to her by her father.

00:34:55.574 --> 00:34:58.726
When she wakes up, her bedroom is on fire, along with the homemade angel

00:34:58.758 --> 00:35:00.438
costume that she was going to wear for Halloween.

00:35:00.534 --> 00:35:03.626
It's interesting that Sienna is a cosplayer, not only because this is

00:35:03.648 --> 00:35:06.766
another type of artist, but the woman from the Terrifier short film was also

00:35:06.788 --> 00:35:08.154
known to be a costume designer.

00:35:08.202 --> 00:35:10.986
It seems that Art's supernatural abilities have been taken up a notch after his revival.

00:35:11.018 --> 00:35:14.282
We knew that he was evil and brutal like Michael Myers before,

00:35:14.346 --> 00:35:18.046
but now he's waking up in body bags like Mark Hoffman and invading

00:35:18.078 --> 00:35:19.326
dreams like Freddy Krueger.

00:35:19.438 --> 00:35:23.054
Not only that, but the fire art started in Sienna's dream somehow became

00:35:23.102 --> 00:35:25.858
real in her bedroom, just like what happened to Kristen Parker in

00:35:25.864 --> 00:35:27.090
A Nightmare on Elm Street 4.

00:35:27.160 --> 00:35:30.006
The point is, Art is more powerful now than ever before.

00:35:30.108 --> 00:35:33.718
It's unclear why Art is going after Sienna specifically, but there is a lot

00:35:33.724 --> 00:35:37.222
of heavy handed good versus evil symbolism going on between Sienna and Art.

00:35:37.276 --> 00:35:40.486
Sienna designed her own angel costume, and Art kills people and lights them on fire,

00:35:40.508 --> 00:35:43.766
kind of tying back into the hell symbolism last seen in the 9th circle.

00:35:43.798 --> 00:35:48.006
Sienna's dad also drew some not so subtle images of a woman in angel

00:35:48.038 --> 00:35:50.582
wings beheading a demon that looks a lot like Art the clown.

00:35:50.646 --> 00:35:53.662
Whatever this actually means, it's clearly some kind of prophecy that Art

00:35:53.716 --> 00:35:55.098
seems to be taking seriously.

00:35:55.194 --> 00:35:58.874
That morning, Art affixes some sharp things to blunt objects in preparation

00:35:58.922 --> 00:36:00.282
for his Halloween festivities.

00:36:00.346 --> 00:36:03.306
While the Pale Little Girl watches Victoria's interview about the Miles

00:36:03.338 --> 00:36:07.394
county massacre on TV, Art gets a kick out of Victoria's mutilated face, but

00:36:07.432 --> 00:36:09.060
doesn't like what she has to say.

00:36:09.990 --> 00:36:13.358
Later that day, they harass Sienna's brother Jonathan at school by tearing

00:36:13.374 --> 00:36:15.582
apart a dead possum and throwing it in his direction.

00:36:15.646 --> 00:36:18.546
Jonathan gets blamed for mutilating the possum corpse, which gets him in

00:36:18.568 --> 00:36:21.206
even deeper trouble with his family, who are already concerned about his

00:36:21.228 --> 00:36:23.970
obsession with serial killers, specifically Art the clown.

00:36:24.050 --> 00:36:26.790
Later, Art stalks Sienna and her friends at a Halloween store.

00:36:26.860 --> 00:36:30.294
He leers at Sienna and creeps her out, but she naturally just assumes that

00:36:30.332 --> 00:36:32.682
somebody dressed as Art the Clown is trying to scare her.

00:36:32.736 --> 00:36:35.622
By the way, if you ever find yourself in this situation, check the teeth.

00:36:35.686 --> 00:36:37.462
Art follows her to the cashier station.

00:36:37.526 --> 00:36:40.878
He tries out sunglasses and various other items, and there's even a little

00:36:40.884 --> 00:36:43.950
bit of a repeat of the first scene that we saw of him from the 9th circle,

00:36:47.090 --> 00:36:47.590
–[Sienna] Please don’t.

00:36:52.412 --> 00:36:53.364
( Art honks his horn in Sienna’s ear)

00:36:53.490 --> 00:36:56.798
He's scolded by the employee and doesn't take kindly to that.

00:36:56.884 --> 00:36:59.666
After locking them in the store, he acts like he's going to buy the horn and

00:36:59.688 --> 00:37:02.994
instead smashes the cashier's face with a bottle, rips out his eye, and

00:37:03.032 --> 00:37:03.762
beheads him.

00:37:03.816 --> 00:37:06.326
He even poses with the cashier's head to have a little fun with some passerby.

00:37:06.348 --> 00:37:07.880
-[Kid] Wow.

00:37:08.570 --> 00:37:09.638
-[Kid] Look at that mom!

00:37:09.804 --> 00:37:11.378
-[Mom] Yeah, that's wonderful, honey.

00:37:11.474 --> 00:37:12.390
Yes. Me.

00:37:12.460 --> 00:37:13.334
That's me.

00:37:13.452 --> 00:37:16.626
Once again, this scene is demonstrating Art's desire to have an audience.

00:37:16.738 --> 00:37:19.030
Next, Art shows up to trick or treat at Allie's house.

00:37:19.100 --> 00:37:22.070
This is Sienna's friend, who he ran into briefly at the Halloween store.

00:37:22.140 --> 00:37:25.274
He doesn't like being told that he's too old to trick or treat, and who would?

00:37:25.312 --> 00:37:28.822
But when Allie notices the real seemingly used weapons in his bag,

00:37:28.886 --> 00:37:31.062
she goes inside and wisely locks her door.

00:37:31.126 --> 00:37:34.478
As usual, Art finds another way, this time smashing the glass door in the

00:37:34.484 --> 00:37:35.870
back and making himself at home.

00:37:35.940 --> 00:37:39.726
Allie freezes upon seeing him, but when he spots her, he decides it's time for

00:37:39.748 --> 00:37:40.910
a little makeover.

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:49.537
(Impact)

00:37:53.726 --> 00:37:57.130
♪ Haunting Music ♪

00:37:57.130 --> 00:38:01.606
After removing Allie's scalp, her back, and her left arm, he rushes back in

00:38:01.628 --> 00:38:04.370
and covers all of her open wounds with bleach and salt.

00:38:04.450 --> 00:38:08.006
Later, Allie's mom returns home to find Art tearing her daughter apart like

00:38:08.028 --> 00:38:09.234
a pick and peel Twizzler.

00:38:09.282 --> 00:38:11.518
And the worst part is she's still alive.

00:38:11.634 --> 00:38:14.730
We know that Art always loves an audience, and that's no different here.

00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:18.198
He literally slaps his knee and laughs in delight at her horror.

00:38:18.294 --> 00:38:21.978
And speaking of audiences, this image, like many of the creepiest scenes of

00:38:21.984 --> 00:38:24.782
Art that I've discussed throughout this video, is a prime example of why

00:38:24.836 --> 00:38:26.346
audiences find him so creepy.

00:38:26.378 --> 00:38:28.490
It's an example of Incongruent Affect.

00:38:28.570 --> 00:38:31.854
In psychology, Incongruent Affect is when a patient's feelings do not match

00:38:31.892 --> 00:38:34.446
up with their appearance or do not match what is appropriate for the situation.

00:38:34.468 --> 00:38:37.714
The term is literally composed of the word incongruent,

00:38:37.752 --> 00:38:40.766
Something that doesn't match up and affect pertaining to one's emotions.

00:38:40.878 --> 00:38:43.874
You might feel it if you saw someone laughing at a funeral or showing no

00:38:43.912 --> 00:38:45.118
emotion during an argument.

00:38:45.214 --> 00:38:47.442
Incongruence stands out to us and bothers us.

00:38:47.496 --> 00:38:50.646
It's a survival mechanism which primarily helps us spot predators who are

00:38:50.668 --> 00:38:51.542
trying to deceive us.

00:38:51.596 --> 00:38:55.151
It's troubling on a human level, and it's jarring when it’s used effectively in movies. 

00:38:55.151 --> 00:38:57.234
Many people find all clowns creepy.

00:38:57.282 --> 00:39:01.580
The painted on smiles don't match the real human mouths underneath them, and that bothers us.

00:39:01.580 --> 00:39:03.958
When there's a real person doing a job to pay the bills

00:39:03.974 --> 00:39:04.646
under that makeup.

00:39:04.678 --> 00:39:07.690
The happiness on the outside doesn't always match the reality that we know,

00:39:07.760 --> 00:39:09.002
so we don't trust it.

00:39:09.056 --> 00:39:10.602
Art takes this to another level.

00:39:10.656 --> 00:39:13.866
You'd expect someone to react to a horribly brutal murder with shock and disgust. 

00:39:13.888 --> 00:39:17.198
So when we see Art the Clown laughing and slapping his knee,

00:39:17.204 --> 00:39:19.151
It gets a reaction out of us on a deeper level.

00:39:19.151 --> 00:39:21.646
If this all sounds familiar, it's because I talked a lot

00:39:21.668 --> 00:39:24.846
about this concept in another episode of Horror History, the one where I

00:39:24.868 --> 00:39:26.694
broke down the history of Michael Myers.

00:39:26.762 --> 00:39:30.094
In Myers' case, the blank expression seen on his mask makes him look

00:39:30.142 --> 00:39:31.934
Stone cold and doesn't mesh

00:39:31.982 --> 00:39:34.818
When combined with the horrible crimes that he's often seen committing.

00:39:34.824 --> 00:39:37.870
He seems clinical or almost indifferent to the horror he creates.

00:39:37.950 --> 00:39:41.366
Art the Clown isn't just indifferent to his insane crimes, he delights in them.

00:39:41.388 --> 00:39:44.642
The whole thing is just amplified by his perfectly placed little hat.

00:39:44.706 --> 00:39:47.846
It's disturbing to the viewer on a visceral psychological level,

00:39:47.868 --> 00:39:48.562
Which is very effective.

00:39:48.626 --> 00:39:51.954
If, say, you're creating a villain to carry a horror franchise.

00:39:52.082 --> 00:39:54.250
That's not the last we see out of Allie's mom.

00:39:54.320 --> 00:39:57.258
Later that night, Art serves trick or treaters candy out of her head.

00:39:57.344 --> 00:40:00.282
It's interesting that Art doesn't kill these trick or treaters or everyone

00:40:00.336 --> 00:40:01.190
he encounters.

00:40:01.270 --> 00:40:03.338
He sometimes even goofs around with kids.

00:40:03.424 --> 00:40:06.158
Michael Myers also spared the lives of some kids that he encountered at the

00:40:06.164 --> 00:40:07.066
school in Halloween.

00:40:07.178 --> 00:40:11.118
So do Michael Myers and Art both have a soft spot for kids?

00:40:11.204 --> 00:40:11.962
Well, Art certainly doesn't.

00:40:12.026 --> 00:40:15.134
He beheaded Timmy and Tia back in 2013, and it wouldn't be long before

00:40:15.172 --> 00:40:17.858
Sienna's little brother Jonathan found himself under attack.

00:40:17.944 --> 00:40:20.962
He started by vandalizing the Shaw family's car, which is pretty light

00:40:21.016 --> 00:40:22.222
stuff by Art's standards.

00:40:22.286 --> 00:40:25.314
It seems like Art wanted Jonathan to be blamed for this, so he used

00:40:25.352 --> 00:40:30.310
believable materials that a teenager would use instead of his usual

00:40:30.970 --> 00:40:32.280
Bodily waste products.

00:40:33.370 --> 00:40:36.646
Sure enough, Jonathan takes the blame while Art waits inside the car while

00:40:36.668 --> 00:40:37.494
the mom cleans it.

00:40:37.532 --> 00:40:40.806
When she finally notices him, Art pulls out a tiny shotgun and blasts her

00:40:40.828 --> 00:40:41.702
head clean off.

00:40:41.756 --> 00:40:45.220
When Jonathan returns home, he finds his mother sitting at the dining room table without a face, 

00:40:45.220 --> 00:40:47.545
and Art does another Bugs Bunny-esque housewife routine.

00:40:48.269 --> 00:40:50.709
Art brutalizes the mom a little more in front of Jonathan before

00:40:50.832 --> 00:40:52.054
chasing him with a syringe.

00:40:52.102 --> 00:40:55.066
Jonathan runs into Sienna's room to retrieve the mysterious sword that she

00:40:55.088 --> 00:40:57.550
got from her dad, but Art catches him and puts him under.

00:40:57.620 --> 00:41:00.558
With the boy and the sword in tow, Art returns to the base camp at the carnival.

00:41:00.564 --> 00:41:03.886
Meanwhile, Sienna is off at a Halloween party, and it seems like

00:41:03.908 --> 00:41:07.018
Art is able to invade her mind the same way that he invaded her father.

00:41:07.114 --> 00:41:09.838
The Pale Little Girl appears to her on the dance floor, which freaks her out,

00:41:09.844 --> 00:41:12.426
Causing her to leave the party with her friend Brooke and Brooke's boyfriend.

00:41:12.458 --> 00:41:16.230
This is part one of Art's plan to lure Sienna to him.

00:41:16.300 --> 00:41:19.378
Part two involves stealing Jonathan's phone and mimicking his voice.

00:41:19.474 --> 00:41:22.278
The two of them act like teenagers making a prank phone call, and they

00:41:22.284 --> 00:41:24.914
convince Sienna that her brother's in trouble at the abandoned carnival,

00:41:24.962 --> 00:41:28.386
instructing her to meet at the Terrifier, a walkthrough attraction decorated

00:41:28.418 --> 00:41:31.866
with imagery of clowns and demons, including one black skinned entity that

00:41:31.888 --> 00:41:33.498
kind of bears a resemblance to Art.

00:41:33.584 --> 00:41:37.866
So which came first, Art the Clown or the Terrifier attraction?

00:41:37.888 --> 00:41:39.226
I think the answer lies in the past.

00:41:39.328 --> 00:41:42.694
The attraction was probably inspired by the same urban legend that inspired

00:41:42.742 --> 00:41:45.222
the short films found on that mysterious VHS tape.

00:41:45.286 --> 00:41:47.226
Either way, this quest keeps Sienna busy.

00:41:47.258 --> 00:41:49.552
So in the meantime, Art attacks Brooke and her boyfriend, who are waiting in

00:41:49.552 --> 00:41:50.420
the car.

00:41:50.420 --> 00:41:53.790
Brooke manages to kick him in the head and escape, but Art isn't far behind.

00:41:53.860 --> 00:41:55.086
Calmly walking after her as always.

00:41:55.108 --> 00:41:58.674
She comes across his lair, another bathroom that Art has

00:41:58.712 --> 00:42:00.382
absolutely decimated with his signature,

00:42:00.446 --> 00:42:01.778
Art was here on the wall.

00:42:01.864 --> 00:42:06.066
As she begs for her life, Art holds his weapon high in one hand, but in the other,

00:42:06.088 --> 00:42:09.186
He's got the jar of acid that he stole from the coroner's office.

00:42:09.288 --> 00:42:11.142
See? I knew he'd find a use for it.

00:42:11.196 --> 00:42:14.514
He throws the acid on Brooke and bashes her ruthlessly, which culminates with Art,

00:42:14.562 --> 00:42:17.238
removing Brooke's beating heart and eating it.

00:42:17.324 --> 00:42:19.814
This is the second example of Art eating his victims.

00:42:19.862 --> 00:42:22.874
And if I had to guess, it's less about nutrition and more about being as

00:42:22.912 --> 00:42:23.946
disturbing as possible.

00:42:24.048 --> 00:42:26.970
Or maybe he just listened to too many Lady Gaga lyrics.

00:42:26.970 --> 00:42:30.143
♪ He ate my heart. ♪

00:42:30.270 --> 00:42:33.386
Art waits in the bathroom for Sienna, who runs in looking for Brooke, and

00:42:33.408 --> 00:42:35.962
upon finding her, becomes Art's newest audience member.

00:42:36.026 --> 00:42:39.658
Art is finally ready to square off with Sienna when Jonathan joins the party

00:42:39.674 --> 00:42:40.366
and distracts him.

00:42:40.388 --> 00:42:43.566
So Sienna takes advantage of this and plunges a nail ridden 2x4 into

00:42:43.588 --> 00:42:44.478
the side of his leg.

00:42:44.564 --> 00:42:47.534
This is Art the Clown's episode of Horror History, but this sibling

00:42:47.582 --> 00:42:49.938
relationship is really the heart of this particular story.

00:42:50.024 --> 00:42:53.650
Art is just a guy who hates Sienna for some intentionally vague reason,

00:42:53.720 --> 00:42:57.086
possibly having to do with good versus evil and her father's drawings.

00:42:57.198 --> 00:43:00.566
But this story is about family dealing with loss and working together as

00:43:00.588 --> 00:43:01.874
siblings, like I suggested early on.

00:43:01.922 --> 00:43:05.074
We're already starting to see Art being used as a generic vehicle

00:43:05.122 --> 00:43:06.482
to tell different types of stories.

00:43:06.546 --> 00:43:09.826
Leone has said in interviews that Terrifier 2 was his first real attempt

00:43:09.858 --> 00:43:11.810
to tell a meaningful story around Art the Clown.

00:43:11.890 --> 00:43:15.018
This isn't just a sign that he is maturing as a filmmaker, it's proof of

00:43:15.024 --> 00:43:18.134
concept that Art has what it takes to carry a franchise and be a lasting

00:43:18.182 --> 00:43:19.990
horror icon like Michael Myers.

00:43:20.070 --> 00:43:22.938
The chase and fight with Sienna and Jonathan continues deeper into the

00:43:22.944 --> 00:43:25.642
Terrifier haunt, where they see all sorts of demonic imagery.

00:43:25.706 --> 00:43:28.826
Art eventually sneaks up on Jonathan by posing as one of the animatronics

00:43:28.858 --> 00:43:30.874
and goes town with his makeshift chain mace.

00:43:30.922 --> 00:43:33.834
When Sienna hears the commotion, she tries to fight back, but eventually

00:43:33.882 --> 00:43:35.934
just crawls on top of her brother to shield him.

00:43:35.972 --> 00:43:37.478
The not so subtle

00:43:37.514 --> 00:43:39.410
Angel vs Demon imagery hits a fever pitch here.

00:43:39.480 --> 00:43:42.366
This is all going on, by the way, in the church scene in the walkthrough attraction,

00:43:42.398 --> 00:43:45.506
But the power dynamics shift when Sienna catches one of his

00:43:45.528 --> 00:43:47.650
attacks and turns his chain back against him.

00:43:47.720 --> 00:43:50.918
Art appears to be finished when Sienna stabs him through the forehead with a fence post, 

00:43:50.924 --> 00:43:54.390
but everyone knows that's not enough to kill Art at this point.

00:43:54.460 --> 00:43:56.982
Art pounces on Sienna from behind and chokes her out.

00:43:57.036 --> 00:44:00.306
He almost finishes her when Jonathan steals his gun from his ankle holster

00:44:00.338 --> 00:44:01.350
and shoots him with it.

00:44:01.420 --> 00:44:04.406
Reality gets blurred here as both Art and Sienna fight to regain consciousness.

00:44:04.438 --> 00:44:07.946
The Pale Little Girl takes the form of Sienna's mother and

00:44:07.968 --> 00:44:09.002
tries to comfort her.

00:44:09.056 --> 00:44:12.046
However, it soon becomes clear that this is just another form of

00:44:12.068 --> 00:44:15.278
hallucinogenic manipulation, as she had seen in her dream and at the

00:44:15.284 --> 00:44:16.506
Halloween party.

00:44:16.698 --> 00:44:18.862
-[Jonathan] Sienna, get away from her.

00:44:18.916 --> 00:44:20.350
-[Jonathan] That's not Mommy.

00:44:21.250 --> 00:44:24.766
Control slips away from Sienna when Art chokes her and throws her into a pit.

00:44:24.788 --> 00:44:28.258
As he looks down on her, her landing position resembles that of a

00:44:28.264 --> 00:44:31.362
fallen angel and the area lights up red like the fires of hell.

00:44:31.416 --> 00:44:33.550
The archetypal roles have now been reversed.

00:44:33.630 --> 00:44:37.406
Within this pit there is yet another pit, kind of like in Dante's Inferno,

00:44:37.438 --> 00:44:39.058
where there are multiple circles of hell.

00:44:39.144 --> 00:44:42.534
There are horns honking and voices wailing from inside the pit, a little

00:44:42.572 --> 00:44:44.642
reminiscent of the hell we saw in the 9th circle.

00:44:44.706 --> 00:44:47.718
He tosses her into the second pit, which sends Sienna back into the

00:44:47.724 --> 00:44:51.046
world of the Clown Cafe, where she drowns in a dunk tank of sorts while the

00:44:51.068 --> 00:44:53.702
zombie kids sing the distorted Clown Cafe theme song.

00:44:53.766 --> 00:44:57.178
Art tries and fails to wake Jonathan up, then just decides to feast on the

00:44:57.184 --> 00:44:57.990
child's legs.

00:44:58.070 --> 00:45:01.946
But his meal is rudely interrupted when Sienna, rejuvenated by her love for

00:45:01.968 --> 00:45:05.190
her brother, returns from the realm of the Clown Cafe and stabs Art with her

00:45:05.200 --> 00:45:06.010
father's sword.

00:45:06.090 --> 00:45:09.322
Once again, Art is on his heels, and he's the one trying to escape.

00:45:09.386 --> 00:45:12.762
He looks up at Sienna standing over him with a knowing look in his eye.

00:45:12.826 --> 00:45:16.270
Sienna's dad drew pictures of Art being beheaded by an angel, and finally,

00:45:16.340 --> 00:45:18.782
Art recognizes that this moment has arrived.

00:45:18.846 --> 00:45:21.986
In fact, I feel like he almost offers his neck up to her right here as he

00:45:22.008 --> 00:45:25.986
flashes one last signature smile before getting his head hacked off.

00:45:26.088 --> 00:45:29.294
After learning of his invincibility the previous year, he's not too worried

00:45:29.342 --> 00:45:30.270
about his mortality.

00:45:30.350 --> 00:45:33.574
Art's lifeless head lays on the ground for a little bit until the Pale Girl

00:45:33.612 --> 00:45:34.822
comes by and picks it up.

00:45:34.876 --> 00:45:38.198
She cradles it like a baby, flashes her own demon eyes at Sienna and Jonathan,

00:45:38.204 --> 00:45:39.958
and takes Art's head away.

00:45:40.044 --> 00:45:43.334
This may suggest that she's actually more than a piece of Art's imagination,

00:45:43.382 --> 00:45:45.722
but my guess is that this will be something answered in a future installment.

00:45:45.776 --> 00:45:49.434
Back at the psychiatric hospital, Art's only surviving girl

00:45:49.472 --> 00:45:52.586
from the first Miles County Massacre, Victoria, is in the middle of some

00:45:52.608 --> 00:45:55.398
kind of episode, and a nurse comments that she's been humming the theme song

00:45:55.414 --> 00:45:56.782
from the Clown Cafe all day.

00:45:56.836 --> 00:45:59.918
She scrawls some disturbing messages all over the walls, using a lot of the

00:45:59.924 --> 00:46:02.718
same words that were carved into the costume designer way back in the

00:46:02.724 --> 00:46:03.694
Terrifier short.

00:46:03.812 --> 00:46:07.582
And lastly, she writes the words Vicki plus Art with a heart around them

00:46:07.636 --> 00:46:10.866
before going into labor, which involves her pulling her own guts out of her stomach.

00:46:10.888 --> 00:46:13.762
When it's all said and done, she sits on the floor of the cell,

00:46:13.816 --> 00:46:17.470
holding the smiling, severed head of Art the Clown like a newborn baby.

00:46:17.550 --> 00:46:20.958
It's one of about a thousand examples of what you've probably noticed is the

00:46:20.984 --> 00:46:23.890
main focus so far when it comes to Art the Clown, the gore.

00:46:23.970 --> 00:46:27.046
In fact, a lot more attention seems to go into making Art as ruthless and

00:46:27.068 --> 00:46:30.454
blood soaked as possible, rather than making his story compelling or even

00:46:30.492 --> 00:46:32.006
making his lore make any sense.

00:46:32.108 --> 00:46:35.034
The Terrifier films almost feel like they're made to be kill counted, which

00:46:35.072 --> 00:46:38.154
doesn't exactly make them easy to analyze for something like Horror History.

00:46:38.272 --> 00:46:41.354
As you probably noticed, I had to do a lot of works to try to make any

00:46:41.392 --> 00:46:44.706
coherent sense of this character, because thematic consistency and logic

00:46:44.758 --> 00:46:47.726
will always be thrown out in favor of a really cool kill.

00:46:47.828 --> 00:46:51.038
Hopefully, the legwork put into this episode helped you appreciate Art in a new light though.

00:46:51.044 --> 00:46:54.094
I obviously like a good story, so I haven't been that

00:46:54.132 --> 00:46:57.006
crazy about the Terrifier movies to this point, but there's something that I

00:46:57.028 --> 00:47:00.078
like about Art, maybe not as a character, but as an icon.

00:47:00.174 --> 00:47:03.458
You can't argue with the fact that these movies have found an audience and

00:47:03.464 --> 00:47:04.290
that's hard to do.

00:47:04.360 --> 00:47:08.066
Leone may have stumbled into something more, and the idea of using Art as

00:47:08.088 --> 00:47:11.174
the main draw in a better thought out story at some point is still pretty exciting.

00:47:11.212 --> 00:47:14.658
It is actually his simplicity that makes him so versatile.

00:47:14.754 --> 00:47:17.202
The same was once true for Michael Myers.

00:47:17.266 --> 00:47:20.406
John Carpenter purposely didn't do much to flesh out this character for his

00:47:20.428 --> 00:47:24.186
audience in the 1970s, he referred to Myers simply as the shape in the

00:47:24.208 --> 00:47:26.714
original script for Halloween, and that's how the character is actually

00:47:26.752 --> 00:47:27.978
listed in the film's credits.

00:47:28.064 --> 00:47:30.358
But Michael Myers doesn't need much backstory.

00:47:30.454 --> 00:47:33.786
We don't need to know anything about him except that he's the embodiment of evil

00:47:33.808 --> 00:47:37.134
And that he hunts Laurie Strode and the people she cares about.

00:47:37.172 --> 00:47:37.754
Like Art the Clown,

00:47:37.802 --> 00:47:41.182
Myers doesn't use words to express himself because he doesn't need them.

00:47:41.236 --> 00:47:44.986
If Michael Myers explained that he was jealous of the attention that Laurie

00:47:45.018 --> 00:47:47.666
got from their parents as a baby or something, we'd know that he was just

00:47:47.688 --> 00:47:49.550
some lame guy driven by hurt feelings.

00:47:49.630 --> 00:47:52.610
Instead, Carpenter let moviegoers ponder these questions on their own.

00:47:52.680 --> 00:47:56.802
Why is Michael Myers so relentlessly evil? Is he human? Or is he something more?

00:47:56.856 --> 00:48:00.034
The fact that we don't have answers for these questions is actually

00:48:00.072 --> 00:48:01.442
what made the character endure.

00:48:01.506 --> 00:48:04.342
Art the Clown scare factor operates the exact same way.

00:48:04.396 --> 00:48:07.298
We don't know what forces are at work to make him invincible, or if it's

00:48:07.314 --> 00:48:08.502
even possible to kill him.

00:48:08.556 --> 00:48:11.394
I kind of want to know what would happen if the people of Miles County

00:48:11.442 --> 00:48:13.142
tossed him into an industrial shredder.

00:48:13.206 --> 00:48:16.454
We still don't know his motivations outside of seeming to have a prejudice

00:48:16.502 --> 00:48:18.758
for women, or why he delights in being so vile.

00:48:18.854 --> 00:48:21.974
Since we don't know anything about him, he could potentially pop up anywhere

00:48:22.022 --> 00:48:23.066
and target anyone.

00:48:23.168 --> 00:48:26.686
Most importantly, he could be placed at the center of any kind of story,

00:48:26.708 --> 00:48:28.826
As long as that story takes place on Halloween.

00:48:28.938 --> 00:48:32.686
The original movie, All Hollows Eve, is even named after the holiday,

00:48:32.708 --> 00:48:35.214
Just like Michael's debut 35 years before.

00:48:35.332 --> 00:48:38.686
For these reasons, Art the Clown really could be the Michael Myers for a brand new generation.

00:48:38.708 --> 00:48:41.994
With a third Terrifier on the horizon,

00:48:42.042 --> 00:48:44.606
This would be a perfect time to check out my Horror history episodes on

00:48:44.628 --> 00:48:45.490
Michael Myers.

00:48:45.570 --> 00:48:48.322
Or if you're still looking to clown, check out my Pennywise episode.

00:48:48.386 --> 00:48:49.798
You'll find that one on the left.

00:48:49.884 --> 00:48:52.902
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:48:52.956 --> 00:48:56.758
Ring the Deathbell for notifications, and I'll see you in the next one,

00:48:56.844 --> 00:48:58.690
Assuming we both survive.

